cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research program, software, experiments, or artifacts, cite the repository and the exact commit used."
title: "SelfState: A Falsifiable Research Program for Self-Equivalent Control State"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lacroix"
    given-names: "Gabriel"
    alias: "EsotericShadow"
abstract: >-
  SelfState is an independent computational research program investigating when
  an adaptive controller benefits from preserving a persistent representation
  of the continuing system that is acting. The project studies decision-relevant
  agent state under partial observability, including action-effect dynamics,
  viability, capability, commitments, recovery, and continuity. It explicitly
  distinguishes self-equivalent control state from generic hidden-state tracking
  and does not claim to detect or produce consciousness.
repository-code: "https://github.com/EsotericShadow/selfstate"
url: "https://github.com/EsotericShadow/selfstate"
keywords:
  - "reinforcement learning"
  - "partially observable control"
  - "state representation"
  - "robot self-modeling"
  - "predictive control"
  - "interoception"
  - "agent state"
  - "causal representation learning"
